WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.170
Week 23: Perfect Tenses and Relevant Past. report experience and recent developments connect past action to present relevance sequence prior events

2
00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:24.951
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can report experience and recent developments, connect past action to present relevance, sequence prior events. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:24.951 --> 00:00:33.414
Language system. Present perfect; past participles; regional preterite/perfect preferences; pluperfect introduction.

4
00:00:33.414 --> 00:00:38.784
Sound and delivery. Participial endings and connected haber forms.

5
00:00:38.784 --> 00:00:48.061
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:48.061 --> 00:01:16.921
Model language. Ya hemos completado la primera fase. — We have already completed the first phase. Todavía no han llegado los datos. — The data have not arrived yet. ¿Alguna vez has trabajado en Chile? — Have you ever worked in Chile? Cuando llamó, yo ya había enviado el informe. — When he or she called, I had already sent the report. La situación ha cambiado recientemente. — The situation has changed recently.

7
00:01:16.921 --> 00:01:26.819
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
